# websocket/ssl tests
leak:mbedtls_ssl_setup
leak:mbedtls_ssl_tls13_compute_application_transform
leak:rsa_alloc_wrap
leak:mbedtls_pk_parse

# sqlite tests
leak:*sqlite*

# v
leak:v__*
leak:os__*
leak:string__plus
leak:malloc_uncollectable
leak:new_array_from_c_array
leak:_vinit

# -prealloc keeps the base arena of a spawned thread until the process exits:
# values that the thread allocated can outlive it (results read by `wait()`,
# channel messages). Only the thread-local block pointer refers to the arena's
# header, so LeakSanitizer reports the header once the thread has ended, and
# gcc 11's LeakSanitizer also the headers of the blocks that the arena grew
# into. A grown block header is always linked from the first block of its arena
# or scope, which stays reported when that arena or scope is lost.
leak:vmemory_block_init_thread
leak:vmemory_block_grow

# A parallel parse reads each source into memory of the C allocator, and the
# buffer of a source whose text the compiler keeps goes to the table of kept
# source texts (flat.FlatAst.source_texts), which keeps it until the process
# exits. That table is in -prealloc arena memory, which is mapped with mmap and
# not scanned by LeakSanitizer, so each kept buffer is reported as a direct leak.
leak:parser__read_batch_source
